{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":185,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:1Thess.3","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"1 Thessalonians","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"1 Thessalonians 3","reference":"1 Thessalonians 3","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"1.","scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":2,"text":"We - Paul and Silvanus.","scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":3,"text":"Could bear no longer - Our desire and fear for you.","scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":4,"text":"3.","scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":5,"text":"We are appointed hereto - Are in every respect laid in a fit posture for it, by the very design and contrivance of God himself for the trial and increase of our faith and all other graces.","scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":6,"text":"He gives riches to the world; but stores up his treasure of wholesome afflictions for his children.","scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":7,"text":"6.","scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":8,"text":"But now when Timotheus was come to us from you - Immediately after his return, St. Paul wrote; while his joy was fresh, and his tenderness at the height.","scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":9,"text":"8.","scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":10,"text":"Now we live - Indeed; we enjoy life: so great is our affection for you.","scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":11,"text":"10.","scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":12,"text":"And perfect that which is wanting in your faith - So St. Paul did not know that \"they who are once upon the rock no longer need to be taught by man.\"","scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":13,"text":"11.","scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":14,"text":"Direct our way - This prayer is addressed to Christ, as well as to the Father.","scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":15,"text":"13.","scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":16,"text":"With all his, Christ's, saints - Both angels and men.","scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"1 Thessalonians","chapter":3}}